Alliance of Independent Physicians
V2 Structural Rules (Spec Freeze)

Version: 2.0
Purpose: Defines new structural, permission, and approval rules before implementation.

1️⃣ Practice Is the Primary Entity

Practices (Clinics) are now the primary searchable and structural unit.

Public directory displays Practices first, not individual doctors.

Each Practice:

Has its own profile page

Has locations, insurance, services

Has multiple doctors

Derives specialties from associated doctors

Doctors cannot exist independently without being associated with a Practice.

2️⃣ Doctor Belongs to Exactly One Practice

Every Doctor must have exactly one practiceId.

No multi-practice membership allowed in V2.

Doctor profile always shows associated Practice.

Doctor cannot be activated without an approved practice association.

3️⃣ Roles & Hierarchy
System Roles

Admin (Highest)

Full system control

Approves all requests

Can edit any doctor or practice

Overrides practice-level decisions

Practice Admin

A doctor who created the practice OR is promoted

Can manage their practice (with approval where required)

Can invite/add/remove doctors (approval required)

Can edit practice details (approval required)

Can manage practice locations, insurance, services (approval required)

Can send announcements to practice doctors

Doctor (Member)

Manages own profile

Sends referrals

Receives referrals

Views practice details

Cannot edit practice

Public

Can search and view practices

Can view doctor public profiles

Cannot see protected data

4️⃣ Dual Approval Model

Certain actions require two layers of approval.

Case A — Doctor joins existing practice

Requires:

Practice Admin approval

Admin approval

Case B — Doctor creates new practice

Requires:

Admin approval only
(Doctor becomes Practice Admin upon approval)

Case C — Practice modifications (edit, location change, roster change)

Requires:

Admin approval
(Practice Admin initiates request)

Approval Tracking Rules

All requests are stored in ApprovalRequest

All decisions logged in append-only ApprovalHistory

Every approval must record:

Who decided

Role

Timestamp

Reason (if rejected)

5️⃣ Contact Visibility Rules
Public (Not Logged In)

Doctor profile shows:

Practice contact info only

Practice phone/email

Personal doctor phone/email hidden

Logged-in Doctor

Can see:

Personal contact info of other doctors

Direct email/phone if available

Logged-in Practice Admin

Same as Doctor

Plus visibility into practice-level contact records

6️⃣ Referrals System (Doctor-to-Doctor)
Sending Referral

Only logged-in doctors can send referrals

Referral includes:

Patient initials (no sensitive data)

Condition summary

Notes

Stored with:

fromDoctorId

toDoctorId

practice linkage

status

Referral Status

new

attended

removed

Referral History (Append-Only)

Every change must log:

Who changed it

Old status → new status

Timestamp

Referral Views

Doctors see:

Sent

Received

History

Practice Admin may see practice-level referral overview (future phase)

7️⃣ Notifications System

Notifications are generated for:

Approval updates

Referral received

Referral status change

Practice roster updates

Admin announcements

Practice Admin announcements

Rules:

Stored per doctor

Append-only

Mark as read capability

No deletion (optional soft hide later)

8️⃣ Chat System (Future-Ready Constraints)

Chat is Phase 2/3 but database must support it.

Required Structural Preparation:

Maintain:

doctorId

practiceId

roleInPractice

Maintain clear permission model

Keep approval logs structured for audit

Chat Types (Future):

Direct Doctor ↔ Doctor

Practice-wide channel (Practice Admin → Practice Doctors)

Global Admin Announcement Channel

Security Constraint:

Chat visibility must respect:

Practice boundaries

Role hierarchy

Active membership only

9️⃣ Membership Rules (V2)

Membership is tied to Doctor account.

Practice Admin dashboard shows:

Membership status of all doctors in practice.

Expiry tracking required.

Membership does not auto-transfer between practices.

🔒 Non-Negotiable Structural Constraints

Every Doctor must have a practiceId

Every approval action must generate a history record

Public cannot access personal doctor contact data

No UI should bypass approval flow

All edits to practice-level data require Admin approval

